{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 130,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has nothing to do with physics, but we're\nall familiar with the nursery rhyme \"London"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4040,
    "dDurationMs": 7420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bridge is falling down, falling down, falling\ndown, London bridge is falling down, and was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11460,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rebuilt in Arizona.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13370,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wait, Arizona?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14650,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "THIS Arizona?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15750,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yup!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16750,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here it is in Lake Havasu City, near artificial\nLake Havasu in the middle of the Arizona desert."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21150,
    "dDurationMs": 2269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "London, I think this merits some explanation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23419,
    "dDurationMs": 4641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, in the early 1800s, when the already\n600-year-old London bridge - that's the one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28060,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that had all of the houses and shops on it\n- was on its last legs, it made sense to replace"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31890,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it with the less-awesome but brand spanking\nnew \"New London Bridge.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35410,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But by the 1960s, this new bridge was barely\neven 130 years old and already needed to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39910,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "replaced because it was sinking into the river\nThames."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42420,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Was the City of London really so short on\ncash that it a) couldn't afford to fix it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45900,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and b) needed to sell the old bridge to fund\na new, even more boring one?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49870,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Apparently so."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51050,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also apparently, when American chainsaw tycoon\nRobert McCulloch actually offered to buy the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55670,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bridge, he though he was bidding on Tower\nBridge (which, while it's often confused with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59280,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "London Bridge by ignorant Americans like me,\nyou'd think you'd do your research if you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63079,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were spending two and a half million dollars\nand buying a bridge)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66159,
    "dDurationMs": 3541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And maybe McCulloch did do his research after\nall, because the Council member from the City"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69700,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of London who was responsible for the sale\nof the bridge claimed that McCulloch knew"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72700,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all along which bridge he was buying."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74320,
    "dDurationMs": 2219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, really, who would admit otherwise?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76539,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anonymous sources from within the City of\nLondon still hint that \"the silly American"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79869,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really thought he was buying Tower Bridge.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81969,
    "dDurationMs": 3290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But whether McCulloch got a bridge he wanted\nor a bridge he didn't but was too ashamed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85259,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to take back for a refund, he brought London\nBridge to the town he had founded in Arizona"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88969,
    "dDurationMs": 3611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so he could have workers for his chainsaw\nfactories, put it back together as a facade"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92580,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "built on land over a concrete frame… and\nthen dug a channel under it and filled it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96850,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97850,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now the New Old New London Bridge lives\nout the rest of its days as an artificial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101090,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bridge in an artificial town on an artificial\nlake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103670,
    "dDurationMs": 22979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh yeah, and it's the third-biggest tourist\nattraction in the State of Arizona."
    } ]
  } ]
}
